==Enemy==
I.M. Phace is the Alien variant of [[The Face]]. Aside from being significantly faster, he also has higher range and a faster attack cycle, topped by his 30% chance to [[freeze]] cats for 2 seconds. At 100% strength magnification, he has 44,444 health and deals 1,333 damage, making him much weaker than his original counterpart. However, he makes up for this with the very high buff that all [[:Category:Unstarred Alien Enemies|unstarred Aliens]] have initially—without any [[anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]], he has over 300,000 HP and deals 9,000 damage, making him 3/4 as strong as [[Teacher Bun Bun]] defensively and just as powerful offensively. Fortunately, his long foreswing gives a pretty wide window of opportunity to time units.

==Strategy==
Make sure to collect the Superior [[Treasure]]s from [[Japan (Into the Future)|Japan]], [[Russia (Into the Future)|Russia]], [[Denmark (Into the Future)|Denmark]], [[Spain (Into the Future)|Spain]], [[Greece (Into the Future)|Greece]], [[India (Into the Future)|India]], [[Cambodia (Into the Future)|Cambodia]] and [[Australia (Into the Future)|Australia]] to activate the [[Aqua Crystal]], or else you'll be fighting him with twice the stats he's supposed to have.

He has a longer-than-average backswing, so he won't be moving much on his own if you bring three or more meatshields (e.g., [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]], [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]]). Do not rely on slow attackers or debuffers that have under 365 range, like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer Cat]] or [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]], as I.M. Phace will usually kill them before they can land a hit. Instead, use units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]]. Dragon Cat and Bahamut Cat can deal heavy damage to him from long range and eventually kill him, while Castaway Cat can freeze him and deal relatively good damage when stacked. When you unlock his [[True Form]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] becomes strong against Aliens, so bring him for his good stats despite him being outranged by I.M. Phace.

Later in the game, though he's still no pushover, he will become less difficult to deal with, as you will have all the Unstarred Alien Treasures and better ranged Anti-Floating/Alien units.

