==Trivia==
*The pronunciation of his English name sounds similar to "I am Face", which might be a spoof of Groot's catchphrase "I am Groot" from the ''[[wikipedia:Guardians of the Galaxy|Guardians of the Galaxy]]'' series.
*His Japanese name, Kaworu-san (カヲルさん), is almost the same as [[The Face]]'s, Kaoru-kun (カオル君), except オ ''o'' is changed to ヲ ''wo'' and the honorific 君 ''-kun'' is replaced with さん ''-san''.
*The mini-Phace inside of his mouth is a reference to the [[wikipedia:Alien (creature in Alien franchise)|Xenomorphs]] from the ''[[wikipedia:Alien (franchise)|Alien]]'' franchise.
*His design is similar to the heads of the [[wikia:dragonball:Namekian|Namekians]] from ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Ball|Dragon Ball]]''. The ears in particular could also be referencing [[wikipedia:Spock|Spock]] and the Vulcans from ''[[wikipedia:Star Trek|Star Trek]]''.
*The hit show in his description, "Face Force 5", may be a reference to the [[wikia:pulpfiction:Fox Force Five|Fox Force Five]] from ''[[wikipedia:Pulp Fiction|Pulp Fiction]]''.
*His Japanese description suggests that the smaller Phace inside his mouth is actually [[The Face]] himself, somehow shrunken down and using the larger Phace as a mobile villa.
*Prior to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] [[Version 12.5 Update|12.5]], the [[Enemy Guide]] entries for I.M. Phace, [[Maawth]], [[Cli-One]] and [[Cosmic Cyclone]] listed their traits as "([[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]], [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]])" instead of "(Alien/Floating)". His name was still listed as "I.M. Phace(Alien, Floating)" until [[Version 13.3 Update|13.3]].

